{"content_hash": "2805979edddb0beb", "version_id": 552, "article_id": 56, "level_code": "en_a2", "lang": "en", "level": 2, "level_label": "A2 初级", "title": "Canadian poet Anne Carson wins Nobel Literature Prize", "title_zh": "加拿大诗人安妮·卡森获得诺贝尔文学奖", "has_translation": true, "topic": "culture", "source": "bbc_culture", "source_url": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cq4g1j54nepyo?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss", "image": {"type": "photo", "url": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1586859411132-573998709aa9?ixid=M3wxMDk3Mzk1fDB8MXxzZWFyY2h8M3x8Ym9sZCUyMGludmVudGl2ZSUyMGNhbmFkaWFufGVufDB8MHx8fDE3OTE2NzgxOTd8MA&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&w=1600&q=75&fm=jpg&fit=max", "provider": "unsplash", "credit": "Photo by Isabel Piñeiro on Unsplash", "author": "Isabel Piñeiro", "credit_url": "https://unsplash.com/@isabelpinheiro?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "source": "Unsplash", "source_url": "https://unsplash.com/photos/red-and-white-flag-on-rock-formation-near-body-of-water-during-daytime-MJFBzRgEqEc?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "fallback": {"type": "gradient", "from": "hsl(250, 42%, 62%)", "to": "hsl(288, 46%, 48%)", "label": "CULTURE", "seed": "45e27dcc686b"}}, "published_date": "2026-10-08", "word_count": 113, "reading_minutes": 0.6, "lead": "Anne Carson is a poet from Canada. She won the Nobel Prize in Literature this year. The prize is for all of her writing.", "lead_zh": "安妮·卡森是来自加拿大的诗人。她今年获得了诺贝尔文学奖。这个奖项是对她全部写作的肯定。", "preview": "Carson is 76 years old. She writes poems, essays and translations. The Nobel committee said her work is bold and new. She mixes old Greek st", "preview_zh": "卡森76岁。她写诗、散文和翻译。诺贝尔委员会说她的作品大胆又新颖。她把古希腊故事和现代写作混在一起。", "has_audio": true, "audio": {"id": 540, "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/56/en_a2.mp3", "duration": 50.175, "size_bytes": 304848, "engine": "edge-tts", "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural", "word_count": 131, "has_timeline": true}, "detail_url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@fc48a26/content/data/versions/552.json", "paragraphs": ["Carson is 76 years old. She writes poems, essays and translations. The Nobel committee said her work is bold and new. She mixes old Greek stories with modern writing.", "Carson was in Iceland when she heard the news. She joked that the judges were \"crazy.\" She said she was surprised but very happy. She was listening to the wind there.", "Carson was born in Toronto in 1950. She lives in Michigan now. She also has Icelandic citizenship. She taught classics for more than 30 years.", "Her famous books include The Glass Essay and Autobiography of Red. The Nobel Prize comes with 12 million Swedish kronor. Canada's prime minister called it a proud moment."], "paragraphs_zh": ["卡森76岁。她写诗、散文和翻译。诺贝尔委员会说她的作品大胆又新颖。她把古希腊故事和现代写作混在一起。", "卡森听到消息时正在冰岛。她开玩笑说评委们“疯了”。她说自己很惊讶，但非常开心。她当时正在那里听风。", "卡森1950年出生在多伦多。她现在住在密歇根。她也有冰岛国籍。她教古典学超过30年。", "她的著名作品包括《玻璃随笔》和《红色自传》。诺贝尔奖奖金是1200万瑞典克朗。加拿大总理称这是骄傲的时刻。"], "body": "Carson is 76 years old. She writes poems, essays and translations. The Nobel committee said her work is bold and new. She mixes old Greek stories with modern writing.\n\nCarson was in Iceland when she heard the news. She joked that the judges were \"crazy.\" She said she was surprised but very happy. She was listening to the wind there.\n\nCarson was born in Toronto in 1950. She lives in Michigan now. She also has Icelandic citizenship. She taught classics for more than 30 years.\n\nHer famous books include The Glass Essay and Autobiography of Red. The Nobel Prize comes with 12 million Swedish kronor. Canada's prime minister called it a proud moment.", "body_zh": "卡森76岁。她写诗、散文和翻译。诺贝尔委员会说她的作品大胆又新颖。她把古希腊故事和现代写作混在一起。\n\n卡森听到消息时正在冰岛。她开玩笑说评委们“疯了”。她说自己很惊讶，但非常开心。她当时正在那里听风。\n\n卡森1950年出生在多伦多。她现在住在密歇根。她也有冰岛国籍。她教古典学超过30年。\n\n她的著名作品包括《玻璃随笔》和《红色自传》。诺贝尔奖奖金是1200万瑞典克朗。加拿大总理称这是骄傲的时刻。", "text": "Carson is 76 years old. She writes poems, essays and translations. The Nobel committee said her work is bold and new. She mixes old Greek stories with modern writing. Carson was in Iceland when she heard the news. She joked that the judges were \"crazy.\" She said she was surprised but very happy. She was listening to the wind there. Carson was born in Toronto in 1950. She lives in Michigan now. She also has Icelandic citizenship. She taught classics for more than 30 years. Her famous books include The Glass Essay and Autobiography of Red. The Nobel Prize comes with 12 million Swedish kronor. Canada's prime minister called it a proud moment.", "vocab": [{"word": "poet", "pos": "noun", "zh": "诗人", "note": "", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "prize", "pos": "noun", "zh": "奖项", "note": "", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "literature", "pos": "noun", "zh": "文学", "note": "", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "bold", "pos": "adj", "zh": "大胆的", "note": "", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "inventive", "pos": "adj", "zh": "有创意的", "note": "", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "translation", "pos": "noun", "zh": "翻译", "note": "", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "citizenship", "pos": "noun", "zh": "国籍", "note": "", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "proud", "pos": "adj", "zh": "骄傲的", "note": "", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}], "title_original": "'Bold and inventive' Canadian poet Anne Carson wins Nobel Literature Prize", "summary_original": "Carson, 76, is celebrated for works that often cross boundaries between poetry, fiction and scholarship.", "body_original": "'Bold and inventive' Canadian poet Anne Carson wins Nobel Literature Prize\nBy\nIan Youngs\nCulture reporter\nPublished\n8 October 2026\nCanadian poet, essayist and translator Anne Carson has been awarded this year's Nobel Prize in Literature.\nCarson, 76, is celebrated for works that often cross the boundaries between poetry, fiction and scholarship.\nThe Nobel Prize committee said they had selected her \"for her bold and inventive oeuvre that, in playful dialogue with the classical tradition, has created new forms for contemporary literature\".\nCarson responded by joking that the judges were \"crazy\" for honouring her. \"I think they're all crazy... Well, you know, it's crazy,\" she told public broadcaster RUV in Iceland, where she is currently staying.\nThe Nobel Prize is awarded for a lifetime's body of work and is regarded as the most prestigious award in global literature, with the winner receiving 12 million Swedish kronor (£900,000, $1.2m).\nIngrid Carlberg, permanent secretary of the Swedish Academy, said she had broken the news to Carson on the phone shortly before the public announcement.\n\"She had time to tell me was that she is, for the moment, in Iceland, where she is listening to the wind,\" Carlberg, said.\n\"She was taken by surprise but very happy. I could hear that in her voice.\"\nBorn in Toronto in 1950, Carson lives in Michigan and has also held Icelandic citizenship since 2022.\nAnders Olsson, chairman of the Swedish Academy's Nobel committee for Literature, praised the way Carson has \"broken away from lyrical poetry bound to the narrative self and inspired new forms of contemporary literature\".\n\"This method of writing leads to playful and ironic works that move not only between classical and modern poetry but also between different genres and artforms,\" he said.\nCanadian Prime Minister Mark Carney said Carson's win was \"an extraordinary achievement and a proud moment for Canada\".\nThe writer's works feature \"wit, imagination, and a style entirely her own,\" Carney wrote on social media.\n\"She has brought ancient stories to new audiences and transformed the way we think about literature.\"\n'Outstanding importance'\nCarson's notable works include The Glass Essay, Autobiography of Red: A Novel in Verse, Nox, Float and The Beauty of the Husband: A Fictional Essay in 29 Tangos.\nIn 2019, her performance piece Norma Jeane Baker of Troy drew a line between famous beauties from different historical periouds - Helen of Troy and Marilyn Monroe.\nIn 2021, she released The Trojan Women: A Comic, a graphic retelling of Euripides' ancient story; and her translation of Elektra by Sophocles was staged starring Brie Larson in London last year.\nShe has been a professor of classics for more than 30 years and her writing is often inspired by Greek literature.\nHer translations have often given a contemporary twist to ancient works.\n\"Her collaborations with visual artists and choreographers and with opera and theatre directors demonstrate the freedom with which she relates to literary expectations and rule systems,\" Olsson said.\n\"It is this that lies behind the outstanding importance her work since the 1990s has had for the international art and literature scene.\"\nRelated topics\nBooks\nLiterature\nNobel Prize\nMore on this story\nHungarian author László Krasznahorkai wins Nobel Literature Prize\nPublished\n9 October 2025\nSouth Korea's Han Kang wins Nobel Literature Prize\nPublished\n10 October 2024\nNorway's Jon Fosse wins Nobel Literature Prize\nPublished\n5 October 2023", "fetched_at": "2026-10-11T00:23:16.183990", "timeline": [{"i": 0, "w": "Carson", "s": 0.1, "e": 0.562, "sm": 100, "em": 562, "cs": 0, "ce": 6, "si": 0}, {"i": 1, "w": "is", "s": 0.575, "e": 0.7, "sm": 575, "em": 700, "cs": 7, "ce": 9, "si": 0}, {"i": 2, "w": "76", "s": 0.713, "e": 0.988, "sm": 712, "em": 987, "cs": 10, "ce": 12, "si": 0}, {"i": 3, "w": "years", "s": 0.988, "e": 1.675, "sm": 987, "em": 1675, "cs": 13, "ce": 18, "si": 0}, {"i": 4, "w": "old", "s": 1.675, "e": 2.087, "sm": 1675, "em": 2087, "cs": 19, "ce": 22, "si": 0}, {"i": 5, "w": ".", "s": 2.087, "e": 2.962, "sm": 2087, "em": 2962, "cs": 22, "ce": 23, "si": 0}, {"i": 6, "w": "She", "s": 2.962, "e": 3.2, "sm": 2962, "em": 3199, "cs": 24, "ce": 27, "si": 1}, {"i": 7, "w": "writes", "s": 3.212, "e": 3.5, "sm": 3212, "em": 3500, "cs": 28, "ce": 34, "si": 1}, {"i": 8, "w": "poems", "s": 3.513, "e": 4.038, "sm": 3512, "em": 4037, "cs": 35, "ce": 40, "si": 1}, {"i": 9, "w": ",", "s": 4.038, "e": 4.225, 